			"Message": "docs(Mist): Restructure README with tables, integration docs, and cleaner layout\n\nRewrite the Mist README to improve readability and provide clearer documentation for the DNS isolation component. Remove the decorative header table with external logos, replacing section headers with plain markdown headings.\n\nKey structural changes:\n- Replace prose feature list with a concise Overview + numbered engineering goals\n- Add 'In the Land Project' section with component integration tables mapping consumers (Mountain, Air, SideCar, Cocoon) to their DNS usage\n- Convert architecture component table and dependency list to markdown tables with consistent formatting\n- Move DNS Zone Configuration, Forward Allowlist, and DNSSEC under a single collapsible subsection\n- Add Security Considerations under zone configuration rather than as a standalone section\n- Rename 'Usage' to 'Getting Started', 'Building & Testing' to 'Build & Test'\n- Add API Reference section linking to rustdoc\n- Replace 'See Also' external links with 'Related Documentation' pointing to sibling component repos (Air, Vine, Mountain) plus local documentation index\n- Replace HTML funding/acknowledgements table with a simpler markdown table and SVG logos\n- Remove Changelog section (now tracked exclusively in CHANGELOG.md)\n- Remove emoji icons from all section headings for consistency\n\nOutcome: README is now scannable, easier to maintain, and clearly situates Mist within the Land architecture.",
